<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cathal mac Finguine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 742</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cathal mac Finguine was king of Munster from about 721 until his death in 742, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eóganacht</a> Glendamnach. He was the most powerful Munster king of his century, invading Leinster and Brega and challenging the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> high kings, and in 737 he met the high king Áed Allán to settle their relations. Later legend portrayed him as a candidate for the high kingship.</p></div>
